 "notes": "Boundary of the union of the solid-line 'confident' spin-down exclusion regions in Fig. 10 (e-print vector figure fabounds.pdf), from X-ray-binary black-hole spin measurements (Cyg X-1, GRS 1915+105, M33 X-7, GRO J1655-40, LMC X-1); the envelope is dominated by Cyg X-1. Axes are mu/eV vs GeV/f, extracted from vector paths calibrated on the axis ticks/gridlines. The excluded region lies BELOW the curve (small 1/f_a = weak self-interaction; large self-interactions quench superradiant spin-down): masses 2.7e-13 to 3.45e-12 eV are excluded for 1/f_a below the m=1 envelope (peak ~6.3e-13 GeV^-1 near mu~3.1e-12 eV), plus a thin m=2 extension up to 6.1e-12 eV at 1/f_a < ~4.5e-18 GeV^-1. The first and last points sit at the plot floor (1/f_a ~ 8e-20 GeV^-1); the exclusion formally extends to arbitrarily small 1/f_a (purely gravitational superradiance). The larger shaded 'could be constrained' regions and the SMBH region (Fig. 11) are not included. The paper quotes no explicit CL; regions are the intersection of spin-down regions over the observational error intervals of the BH parameters ('high confidence'); confidence_level=0.95 is nominal. No dependence on local DM density.",
